WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.040
Hank: Good morning, John.

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.020
I'm in a car! I'm headed to work!

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.720
I'm stopped at a stoplight right now; I'm being
safe.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.120
And I wanted to take you with me to work.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.500
I wanted to show you some of the people who work on the things and the place where they do it.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.720
Here we are. It's work.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.400
Hank: We're gonna start with Matthew.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.120
What are you doing right now?

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.260
Matthew: Finacial Diet
Hank: Hey there's those girls

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.579
Matthew: There they are.
Hank: 'Sup!

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.579
Matthew: They can't answer you.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.260
Hank: How are you doing?

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.260
Nick: Good, how are you?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.260
Am I talking to the camera?

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.579
Hank: I'm at the same spot as the cameraman.

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:44.159
Nick: Yeah, I know, but if I look...

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.520
Eyelines's weird, man. Eyeline!

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.580
Hank: Oh, Nicole's here?
Matthew: Yeah.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.880
Hank: I'll just pretend that she was here
the whole time. Hey, Nicole!

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.180
Nicole: Hi, I've here the whole time.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:53.120
Hank: Who are you editing?
Nicole: Myself.
Hank: Yeah, I know what that's like.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.440
Hank: Ceri's here.
Ceri: Hello.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.600
Hank: What are you writing about right now?

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.219
Ceri: Uh, I'm actually editing Crash Course
Film.

00:00:58.219 --> 00:00:59.219
Hank: This is Alyssa's...

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:01.510
This is Alyssa's sad empty desk, because she
lives in New York sometimes.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:02.510
Hank: Caitlin's here.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.690
Caitlin: Hi! How's it going?
Hank: Good. How are you?

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.540
Caitlin: I am reading about ways to start
a new job.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.030
(Hank laughs) Not because I'm looking for
a new job, but because I'm working a script for How to Adult.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.830
Hank: Thanks for making that clear.
Caitlin: Yeah.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.850
Hank: I'm coming in.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.400
Hank: You're our newest person.
Marcus: I am.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.040
Hank: How are you doing?

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.700
Marcus: I'm learning how to edit you right
now.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.620
Well, um, more specifically, I'm learning
how to animate on top of you.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:37.740
Hank: You wouldn't think there's anything
happening in the darkness over here...

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.740
...but there is.
Michael: Oooh, the darkness.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.420
Hank: Look at you. This is the darkest I have ever seen it in here.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.700
Behind this door is the scariest part.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.260
Oooooooh.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:46.760
Hank: Hey, it's Henry!

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.520
Henry: Hey, are you doing a tour?

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.040
Hank: I am.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.160
So you are... you don't work for me, but you
work in my office.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.340
Henry: This is my office. I rent it from—I rent it from you.
Hank: Right, sorry.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.160
Henry: You crossed into my office.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.840
This is the light that they turn purple when
we're filming.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.920
Hank: This is Marie Ann, who is my assistant. Assists me with all the things. Hi.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.160
Marie Ann: Hello.
Hank: What are you working on?

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.940
Marie Ann: Your emails.
Hank: Thanks. How are they?

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:05.740
Marie Ann: There's lot of them.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:06.940
Oh, look! There's a Julie!

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:07.720
Hank: Hey, it's Julie!

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:08.880
Julie: Hello!

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.200
Hank: What's your official title?

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.360
Julie: Director of Operations.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.160
Money maker.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.620
Hank: The vast majority of the pictures on
this phone...

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.659
Julie: Ooooh!

00:02:16.659 --> 00:02:17.900
His cheeks are coming in, nice!

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:18.900
Julia: Hi!

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.220
Hank: This is Julia. How are you doing?

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.400
Julia: I'm good. How are you?

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.600
Hank: Good. Just maps of Amsterdam and Melbourne?

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:24.600
Julia: Yeah, I gotta think about them.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.480
Hank: We noticed yesterday that you haven't
updated your calendar collection.

00:02:27.489 --> 00:02:28.959
Amy: Funny you say that...

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:31.030
(Hank gasps) Calendar.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.030
Calendar.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.030
Cows doing Yoga.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.030
Rivers. Ocean.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.020
Uh, available on DFTBA, unless it's sold out...

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.470
Hank: Not anymore. We're sold out now.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.710
Amy: Montana Wildlife, and some more Montana.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.100
Hank: That's... That's even more than you had last year!

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:42.700
Amy: I know.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.240
What a cool room you guys have.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.250
Hank: Hey, what are you working on?

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.860
Valerie: I'm working on signage for Nerdcon:
Nerdfighteria.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.020
Hank: Oh, do you have program there behind it?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:50.780
Valerie: Oh, yeah.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.359
Hank: Ooh, oh, ooh, aaah, oh dang!

00:02:53.359 --> 00:02:56.860
Hank: Okay, I'm gonna take pictures of all
of you, and put you on my video.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.380
You're gonna have lower thirds.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.100
Valerie: That's a lot of work for yourself.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.340
Hank: Oh hey, why are you on the floor?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.280
Rodney: Hi Hank.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.340
Natalie: Hello.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.659
Hank: I stopped for whatever this is.

00:03:09.659 --> 00:03:12.049
Now, I'm going to the warehouse.

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:15.809
I get the feeling that our break table isn't
being used very much right now.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.720
Oh, you've—you're already in the video.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.220
Victoria: Hi.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.380
It's pretty out.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.459
And now I go home.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:26.459
It's weird, right?

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:30.110
I want to be clear that, like, Vlogbrothers,
still just me.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:35.330
But all the other things—Vidcon, Scishow,
Crash Course, DFTBA.com, all that stuff—so

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.760
many people are necessary to make it happen.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:42.269
I like doing the business thing, and I like
doing it not in the normal ways.

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:45.709
So I'm gonna keep doing that, and I am excited
for what the future has to hold.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:50.129
There are lot of people who work on the things
that we do, and I am always amazed by them.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.909
And really lucky to have them in my life.

00:03:52.909 --> 00:03:54.220
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

